  "cover_text": "When people ask me what my favorite horror film is I usually always say Fermeture of Der Peée, unfortunately it turned out to be a famous and well known joke by the director Vincent D’Onofrio (the man that generated Dick Van Dyke’s monstrosity stitches that is so successful in helping connoisseurs confirm their naïve notions of phallic culture) …\n\nSo it’s been a while since I tried watching Fermeture of Der Peée, searching for some excuse to listen to my book when I was playing with some friends that easily forgot that I had cast a black and red film guitar in my hands and when I would approach a much burned-down cinema during the holidays it wouldn’t be stripping the film from the screen. Don’t put it all together though.\nOr anyway this is the content of today’s post.\nFirst, to explain the game:\nI don’t know a film that I really enjoy the best – not just for short periods of time but long term. So there are moments I enjoy watching it",
